## What is built and working

- **Leads**: CSV/XLSX import with preview, phone normalisation to E.164, dedup, consent fields, import batches as first-class objects with multi-batch selection and outcome filters, admin-only filtered CSV export.
- **Compliance**: federal DNC import, internal DNC, per-state calling hours (all 51 jurisdictions ship as unreviewed placeholders), `scrub()` gate that no path can bypass.
- **Dialer**: scheduler triggering Retell calls, caller ID rotation, concurrency and daily caps, a daypart-rotating retry ladder, paused by default after every restart.
- **Webhook**: signature-verified, idempotent, handles out-of-order events, maps dispositions, auto-adds do-not-call requests, creates the customer and session on transfer.
- **Verifier workspace**: 16-question checklist, transfer readiness gate, AI pre-fill suggestions kept separate from confirmed answers.
- **Closer workspace**: My Queue with a "Take this call" button visible to every eligible agent, atomic claim lock, appointed-states enforcement, floor-wide banner naming who is on a call, waiting-age badges, outcome capture including "application submitted → pending carrier → approved/declined".
- **Sessions**: scoped per user; admin sees everyone with day/week/month and per-person filters, enforced server-side across six channels.
- **Dashboard**: campaign tiles counting every source, a dialer-scoped funnel, per-user tables measured against the team median (never "best/worst" labels), sample sizes beside every rate.
- **Analytics**: contact rate by day/hour in the lead's timezone, caller ID health vs each number's own baseline, speed to lead, cost per acquisition by vendor. Costs are stamped when they happen, never recomputed.
- **Recordings**: stored server-side in dated folders split by verifiers / licensed agents / approved sales, filenames use customer name + last four digits of phone + username, per-user access enforced server-side.
- **Operational**: live websocket updates that never clear a form being typed in, presence warnings, auto-release of sessions held by a disconnected agent after a 3-minute grace period, admin force-release, git history, a linter, 20 test suites.
- **Login page**: dark lamp scene with a pull cord that reveals the sign-in card.

## Audit already done

A seven-pass pre-launch audit found and fixed 7 blockers, 16 serious and 7 minor issues. `docs/PRE_LAUNCH.md` holds the full record and the go-live checklist. The worst finding: the app had two canonical phone formats and didn't know it, so one person could become two un-matchable records — dangerous for a DNC-sensitive business. Migration 010 repaired it. A later pass found that `sessions:get` was returning any session to any authenticated caller by sequential id, and the export was built on that read.

## Decisions already made — please don't reverse these without asking

- Re-pooling leads **grants** extra attempts, never resets `attempts_count` — that count is a compliance record of how many times a real person was telephoned.
- Campaign tiles count every source; only the funnel is scoped to dialer-originated calls.
- Rates are never computed from samples too small to mean anything; users are compared against the team median, never ranked as best/worst.
- Nothing bypasses `scrub()` — no bulk action, no callback, no manual dial.
- Caller IDs live in their own table so a number can be retired without losing its history.
- Recording filenames use the last four digits of the phone, not the full number.
- Every prompt to Claude Code must end with an instruction to test and verify in the real browser and reconcile on-screen numbers against the database.

